title: SEN CONNECT

**Visual Schedule and Social Story Builder** — An Offline, Bilingual (Urdu/English) 
AI Application for Learners with Autism Spectrum Disorder and Developmental Disabilities

## Project Abstract

Children with Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD) and other developmental disabilities in 
Pakistan face two problems at once: a shortage of individual, evidence-based tools 
(such as visual schedules and Social Stories), and a lack of software that works 
reliably without stable electricity or internet, in the learner's own language. 
This project presents SEN-Connect, an offline-first, bilingual (Urdu/English) mobile 
application built around three connected modules: (1) a Visual Schedule Builder that 
gives learners predictable, picture-based routines; (2) a Social Story Builder that 
lets teachers and parents create narrated, illustrated stories targeting one specific 
behavior, and automatically logs behavior frequency before and after each story; and 
(3) an on-device conversational chatbot, trained only on autism-support content, that 
answers teacher and caregiver questions and helps generate schedules or stories through 
natural conversation — in English or Urdu, without any internet connection. The project 
also includes a Behavior Therapy module for structured ABC (Antecedent-Behavior-Consequence) 
tracking, all running fully offline on a standard Android tablet.
